Overlay patch 0065 (VR R18-A): the class probe's brackets around the
PARTICLES (src/code_80057C60.c only -- no earlier patch owns this file, so
this is a new patch rather than a revision; traps D18/D22).

the user, on 1.0.0.16: "when i use a mushroom, there's still distracting smoke
and gold dust, which seems to follow where my diverging 2nd shadow is." The
round's first deliverable is a per-object-class table measured walk by walk
(overlay 0044 rev15): each class's drawn position against the eye recovered
from the composed eye matrix. 0054 rev6 brackets the shadow, the kart quad and
the boost flash in render_player; this brackets every per-slot particle draw
in render_kart_particles' two helpers:

  func_8006D474  pool 0 (smoke_dust), pool 3 (smoke_dust2: boost sparks, wall
                 bonk stars, ...), pool 1 (smoke_dust3: drift, ground, grass)
  func_8006DC54  pool 0 type 7

Each draw is wrapped in G_NOOP 0x70/0x71 with l = (class << 12) | key, class 4
for the local player's particles (playerId 0, screen 0) and 7 for everybody
else's, key = (playerId << 8) | (pool tag << 4) | slot. 0044 rev15 takes the
first modelview load inside the bracket (func_800652D4's AddEffectMatrix) as
that particle's drawn position. A slot with nothing to draw emits an empty
bracket, which 0044 ignores.

Emitted ONLY while the dev knob gSohVRClassProbe is set; every shipped build
and every flat frame emit nothing, so the display list is byte-for-byte
unchanged and the macOS build compiles none of it (__IOS__).


--- a/src/code_80057C60.c
+++ b/src/code_80057C60.c
@@ -12,6 +12,30 @@
 #include "camera.h"
